{
  "about": [
    "The hub's frozen sync wire fixture, version 5 (D-H0BZN in rdy-design, p-1FPMG in rdyhub-design): the dump of a hub repo and the restore from a dump. Versions 1, 2, 3a and 4 stay beside it, and hold the other steps' cases.",
    "Each step holds one request to the real hub and the hub's reply, as the test dp9_ in rdyhub-server/tests/pg_dp9_wire_v5.rs checks them, in the order the test sends them. The step dumps.create and the step dumps.show are hub operations of the API, which a client calls before the sync step dump (i-W9RPP).",
    "Normalized: the bearer token of ana is <token>, and that of bo is <other-token>; each request id is <request-id>; the dump's id is <dump> and its job's id is <job>, also inside a path or a text; the times end and expires_at of dumps.show are <end> and <expires-at>; the repo id of the view fixture's project, which is new on each run, is <repo-id>. Object members are in key order.",
    "The hub repo is acme/docs, owned by ana, on a test install with Share on, artifact storage and its default sync settings. bo is a member of acme, so bo reads acme/docs, and bo did not start the dump. acme/empty, acme/views and acme/later are hub repos of ana with no store and no hub canon.",
    "The landings are those of rdyhub-core's push fixture, whose repo id is the same on each run. Before the first step, a canon push seeded hub canon in acme/docs with the history of the second landing of the chain and its tag v1.0.0 (version 2 holds that write's form).",
    "The dump job made the dump of acme/docs on the hub's job pool. A binary body gives its length and its sha256: the sync step dump gives the whole dump file, whose sha256 is the one shown, and the digest of dumps.show is rdy core's trailer digest of that file, not its sha256.",
    "Each restore puts one batch: the canon history of the dump's tip, which a temporary holder exports after it loads the downloaded dump. A restore sends no render inputs and no gate settings, because a hub dump holds neither (r-Z4TS8), and names the tag that the batch carries.",
    "Before the restore into content, a canon push moved hub canon of acme/docs to the third landing of the chain, which the dump does not hold, so the restore replaces it as a force push.",
    "The restore into acme/views and its view writes use rdyhub-core's view fixture, a project whose view draft has two writes and a close on canon's first landing; its hashes are the same on each run. Its batches are those that a restore of that project's dump sends, put before each write: first the canon history of canon's tip, then the view's history. Each view write sends null render inputs, as a restore's view writes do (i-B40VF).",
    "The restore of another project puts a batch of rdyhub-core's public fixture, a project with another repo id; the put step refuses it.",
    "The write in read-only mode came after its batch was put, while the operator had read-only mode on.",
    "The list headers names the request headers that the hub reads on these steps. The list not_served is empty: this hub serves each case that version 4 of this file left out."
  ],
